s that require schools to tell parents.\"\n- **His vote:** Lackey is on the Noes list for the Assembly's final concurrence vote (2024-06-27, 61-16). The vote is `in-term`. It isn't `near-unanimous`, since about 20% voted No. Both pages are coded as one `vote` record. The actor and tally quotes come from the vote page, and the provision quote comes from the bill text.\n- **Why it stays blank:** A No on a single-subject bill rules out rung 2 and puts him on the side of telling parents. It can't separate rungs 3, 4 and 5 (tell parents when they ask, notify parents, or require parental permission). The codebook calls a No that only rules out one end `direction-only`.\n- **Still needed:** His own words, or a bill he authored or sponsored, that names one of rungs 3–5. I listed this under `needs_source`.\n\nThere are no candidate quotes. Neither source contains Lackey's own words.","ttft_ms":8376,"type":"result","duration_ms":25306,"uuid":"7191827c-76cb-4fef-a797-99ff706b0055","ttft_stream_ms":2400,"time_to_request_ms":690,"first_content_frame_ms":2401,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
